					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-131954#post-4356039</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-131954/duke-till-dawn#post-4356039</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 08 Sep 2019 20:38:57 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>EnderProph</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3039202</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Alright, so, <em>Duke Till Dawn</em> is&#8230;.</p> <p>controversial, to say the least. People either LOVE 2008-2011(ish) era LolFoundation stuff, or absolutely ABOMINATE it. This isn't some new or novel insight by any stretch of the imagination, but one I feel perinate to mention. <em>Duke Till Dawn</em> is the most iconic tale of the Author Avatar era (well, maybe <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/incident-239-b-clef-kondraki">Incident-239-B</a> is more iconic, but that's debatable, and a discussion for another time), so its the story everyone likes to point at to criticize it. And there's a LOT to critique here. Despite <strong>DESTROYING SITE-19</strong>, potentially releasing hundreds of <strong>WORLD ENDING ABBERITIONS AGAINST SCIENCE, NATURE, AND GOD HIMSELF</strong> into the world, Dr. Kondraki isn't punished in any way in this tale (yes I know in other tales he gets killed for doing shit like this but <em>that wasn't in the original, so it doesn't count</em>). The only people who seem genuinely upset at this are the O5 council (who are &quot;The Man&quot;, and therefor <em>lame</em>), Dr. Iceberg (who just wants Kondraki's job) and maybe Dr. Clef (who, depending on the writer, either hates Kondraki with a fiery passion, is a massive troll, or <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">is the worlds largest tsundere who has the hots for Kondraki</span>). To say that Dr. Kondraki is a Mary Sue is like saying the Sun is mildly warm. And despite all that&#8230;</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>I give it a +1.</p> <p>What can I say? I enjoy wacky hijinks sometimes, and this hits the spot. An <em>absolute madman riding the biggest, baddest motherfucker at the time like a rodeo bull to destroy Discount Drac, logic, rules, and consequences be damned</em> is fun to read. Shoot me.</p> <p>That being said, I think we can mostly all agree, at this point, that it was for the greater good that this stuff got the boot. Thankfully, when we need a bit of old Wacky Hijinks, we can come back to the old LolFoundation stuff and have a laugh.</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Thanks for coming to my Ted Talk, have a nice day.</span></p> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
