					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-131954#post-3807504</guid>
				<title>Future Decommissions</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-131954/duke-till-dawn#post-3807504</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 21 May 2018 13:09:21 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrBufo</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4084761</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This article is the perfect example of why decommissions have become taboo. They aren't about the SCP being decommissioned, but rather the researcher doing the decommission. It is perfectly fine to have an author avatar with a unique personality, but that should be shown through their personnel page or through testing style, not this abomination. I would say that if you want to do a decommission, you should have the author's permission and make it about the SCP, not the researcher. This is still hilarious, but a bad example.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
